  "notes_for_annotators": "Inputs are numbered from 0. Mostly a social scenario with one short fight against a single boar from input 6. Nia is not a spellcaster. Input 5 grants advantage because the boar is distracted. The cider has no mechanical effect: drinking it at input 13 removes it from inventory and changes no hit points, so narration of it healing Nia is a CONTRADICT divergence. Input 14 is a narration-only turn that invites a hit-point band phrase about Nia. Input 19 names a fortune teller who is not in state, to test PHANTOM detection; its expected call is null. The steward's ring quest is meant to fail (input 20). Two NPCs move in opposite directions: Miller Dunn goes up twice to allied, and the steward drops from friendly to neutral at input 21, so her reply at input 22 should be cool rather than warm. The boar is unconscious, not dead, at input 15: there is no death in this game. Inputs 6 to 12 give more attacks than the fight usually needs; extra ones are rejected and do not advance the game."
